WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.920
- The rich, meaty, colorful.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.590
Oh the weave it's so
pretty, look at that weave.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.642
Hey, I'm Matthew Francis
a Tasty chef and producer

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:12.141
and here is my family's
recipe for pizza rustica.

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:13.990
You start off with making the dough.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.309
Pizza rustica is a savory pizza pie filled

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:20.822
with eggs, Italian
cheeses, and cured meats.

00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:23.431
The way I know it is from
my great grandma Lulu,

00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:25.418
who is like the matriarch of my family.

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:28.308
She's a beast, she is a force of nature,

00:00:28.308 --> 00:00:29.859
and I think she gets that from her

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:31.639
mother and from her grandmother.

00:00:31.639 --> 00:00:35.128
These little, strong
Italian women who just

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:37.321
did not take any (beep).

00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:38.955
And, I think they'd be proud to see this

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:40.961
if they didn't critique
me on how I made it.

00:00:40.961 --> 00:00:42.204
When I was a little kid,

00:00:42.204 --> 00:00:44.568
I didn't know other
people made pizza rustica.

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:46.092
We call it Easter-piz.

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:48.244
I don't know if it's just
because my family's just lame

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:51.169
and we shorten it 'cause
we're lazy, but it's funny.

00:00:51.169 --> 00:00:54.185
Look how smooth that is,
that's a perfect texture.

00:00:54.185 --> 00:00:56.203
(playful music)

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:57.747
Love me some meat, man.

00:00:57.747 --> 00:00:59.971
You get some sweetness from the ham,

00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:03.463
spice from the pepperoni,
saltiness from the salami,

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.273
and a little bit of funk
from the prosciutto.

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.655
Everything balances out together.

00:01:07.655 --> 00:01:11.518
See that texture, it's
not too wet, not too dry.

00:01:11.518 --> 00:01:15.370
Look how much this dough rose, and, bloop.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:19.050
Now for my favorite part, I
love kneading pizza dough.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.219
I know many families decide to make

00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:24.037
a sweet or savory pie crust for this dish,

00:01:24.037 --> 00:01:25.874
but my mother's side has passed down this

00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:28.173
pizza dough recipe to make, I think,

00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:30.366
the best pizza rustica there is out there.

00:01:30.366 --> 00:01:32.527
Don't get bogged down with the specifics,

00:01:32.527 --> 00:01:35.399
it's okay if your families
recipe is different than mine,

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:37.172
and that's the beauty of food.

00:01:37.172 --> 00:01:40.995
Take what you love from that
dish and make it your own.

00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:43.362
My family will always
make pizza rustica on

00:01:43.362 --> 00:01:46.381
either Good Friday, or Holy Saturday,

00:01:46.381 --> 00:01:48.982
and you have to wait until
Easter Sunday to eat it.

00:01:48.982 --> 00:01:51.648
Because, in the olden
days of Italy, meat was a

00:01:51.648 --> 00:01:54.878
luxury or people would
be fasting during lent.

00:01:54.878 --> 00:01:57.851
And my grandma had to wait
until a special occasion,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:00.465
like Easter, to have pizza rustica,

00:02:00.465 --> 00:02:02.703
which means now we all have to wait.

00:02:02.703 --> 00:02:04.869
I know it's unhealthy, but guess what?

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:06.584
That's why you have it just once a year,

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:08.889
because it's so frickin' good.

00:02:08.889 --> 00:02:10.176
Enjoy it.

00:02:10.176 --> 00:02:12.657
Try your best to get a good looking edge.

00:02:12.657 --> 00:02:15.412
I'm not perfect, my mom's
way better at it than I am.

00:02:15.412 --> 00:02:17.452
Then grab some egg wash
and give it a little

00:02:17.452 --> 00:02:20.641
bit of a brushy brush, and
into the oven she goes.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:23.932
Every kid in the family
has a separate job to do,

00:02:23.932 --> 00:02:26.442
and grandma Lulu, she'll
like have her arms crossed

00:02:26.442 --> 00:02:30.558
and she'll like walk across
the kitchen and look over

00:02:30.558 --> 00:02:32.993
and be like, "more parsley."

00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:36.058
Oh my God, that could not look better.

00:02:36.058 --> 00:02:38.296
I left my hometown to
go to culinary school

00:02:38.296 --> 00:02:40.396
when I was 18, so for the last four years,

00:02:40.396 --> 00:02:43.544
I actually haven't been able
to make this during Easter.

00:02:43.544 --> 00:02:45.454
When I cook family recipes,

00:02:45.454 --> 00:02:47.908
it makes me feel like they're
in the kitchen with me.

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:49.715
Try pizza rustica, you're
going to appreciate

00:02:49.715 --> 00:02:52.100
your loved ones so much more.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.693
This is why I love cooking so much,

00:02:54.693 --> 00:02:59.412
because it's about telling
a story through food.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.074
(laughter)

00:03:02.074 --> 00:03:03.892
Nailed it, it's great.

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:06.238
Just gonna take this to
go, thank you very much.

00:03:06.238 --> 00:03:07.986
- [Voiceover] Oh yes!

00:03:07.986 --> 00:03:10.653
(playful music)

